WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.509
The one piece manga just kicked off the first
MAJOR battle of the final saga with Luffy

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:09.780
fighting a marine admiral for the FIRST TIME
in over FIVE.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:10.780
HUNDRED.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.780
CHAPTERS!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.890
On top of that this secret agent has betrayed
the straw hats once again and is trying to

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:23.760
kill the genius scientist Dr. Vegapunk, but
he is now facing Zoro who has the chance to

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.380
prove to us just how powerful he truly is.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.200
And all of this is leading to the MASSIVE
conclusion of this arc, which we were told

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:37.950
will completely shock the entire world, and
I have some ideas of what this event could

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.950
actually be.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:44.180
But we of course have to kick off this review
with the epic clash between Luffy and marine

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.500
admiral Kizaru.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:50.230
Because even though we barely get a glimpse
of it in this chapter, the start of this fight

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:55.640
confirms that Luffy will be taking on the
strongest opponent the world government is

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.690
sending to the island.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:02.950
And this is a huge moment for Luffy to show
us just how far he has come since the last

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.939
time he faced marine admirals.

00:01:04.939 --> 00:01:10.070
Because in case you’ve forgotten let’s
take a look at exactly how much Luffy has

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.280
been crushed by the admirals in the past.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:18.110
First, he met admiral Aokiji and was completely
frozen to the point of nearly dying.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.280
The next clash came during the chaos of the
Sabaody arc, where admiral Kizaru was sent

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.310
to take out the straw hats after Luffy punched
the celestial dragon.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.100
And although he never directly clashed with
Luffy, the light-man was super close to taking

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.679
out the entire straw hat crew.

00:01:32.679 --> 00:01:38.299
But then we reached the legendary war at marineford,
where Kizaru took an active role to stop Luffy

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:39.299
from freeing Ace.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:45.670
In fact, he shot Luffy with a laser beam,
sent him flying with a light speed kick twice,

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:50.130
and then sniped the key to Ace’s handcuffs
right out of Luffy’s hands.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:55.130
But that’s not even the worst an admiral
has done to Luffy because at the end of the

00:01:55.130 --> 00:02:01.210
war admiral Akainu killed his brother Ace,
which ABSOLUTELY BROKE Luffy.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:06.480
So yeah, Luffy has A HUGE score to settle
with these marine admirals.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:10.860
Which makes this fight even more interesting.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.540
Because on top of the actual battle to save
the Vegapunks and escape from the island,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.630
there are both personal and world-altering
stakes at play.

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.660
So let’s actually go through all the scenarios
of what could happen based on the outcome

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.660
of this fight.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:32.410
First off, no matter what I don’t think
this will be an easy fight.

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:39.450
Kizaru is one of the OG admirals and his devil
fruit is INSANELY POWERFUL.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:46.280
Plus he is sure to show off haki abilities
that he has never shown before.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:52.920
But Luffy now has awakened his devil fruit
plus learned advanced forms of haki.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:03:00.040
And honestly, after defeating Kaido I think
that Luffy should be able to defeat Kizaru.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.459
Personally, I’ve always powerscaled the
Yonko a bit higher than the admirals, so since

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:11.350
Luffy defeated Kaido then theoretically that
should make him stronger than Kizaru.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:16.610
And if this were to happen, it would certainly
be a huge blow to the World Government as

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:22.440
it would be the first time an admiral was
actually defeated by a pirate in the story.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:27.549
And no I’m not including the fight with
Greenbull at the end of Wano, which never

00:03:27.549 --> 00:03:30.810
really got finished.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:37.140
So this outcome would make Luffy’s reputation
skyrocket even more and significantly weaken

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.290
the overall threat of the marines.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:45.239
However, as we all know, fights in One Piece
are HEAVILY dependent on matchups.

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:52.180
So just because one character should be stronger
than the other doesn’t mean they will win.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.300
Though honestly, Kizaru’s fighting style
and devil fruit abilities don’t seem like

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.579
the type that would give Luffy trouble.

00:03:58.579 --> 00:04:05.299
It’s nothing crazy tricky or confusing such
as the slow beams that nearly caused Luffy

00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:07.599
to lose in Long Ring Long Land.

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:13.409
Essentially Kizaru fights by shooting light
beams, making a light sword, or attacking

00:04:13.409 --> 00:04:17.840
with light speed kicks and punches.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:23.040
All of these are extraordinarily powerful,
but pretty straight forward attacks.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:27.860
And especially with Luffy’s awakening, I’m
wondering if he will be able to grab the light

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.860
attacks and throw them back, similar to how
he caught the lightning during Wano.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:38.250
Plus since he can now make the environment
rubber, he should be able to bounce any light

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.610
beams back pretty easily.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:50.790
So all this means Luffy could be defeating
Kizaru by the end of the arc.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:57.990
However, I personally think the most likely
outcome here will be a draw.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:04.539
It is classic Oda style to show us a clash
of two powerful characters and then something

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:08.860
happens to disrupt the fight.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:13.351
So since Luffy’s main goal here is just
to escape with his crew and new friends, I

00:05:13.351 --> 00:05:18.590
could easily see the fight with Kizaru ending
early and then the straw hats escaping off

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:19.590
the island.

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:25.130
Plus I don’t think Kizaru has the personality
to hunt them down, as long as he can complete

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:30.100
his mission of retrieving the Vegapunk tech,
which we’ll talk more about in just a minute.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:36.080
But if we are considering a Luffy win and
a draw, then we also must think about what

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.160
would happen if Kizaru wins this fight.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:46.020
Because we have actually never seen Kizaru
go all out in a fight, so he may have been

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.710
holding back all this time.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:55.800
And maybe he overwhelms Luffy with his speed
and power, and if this were to happen it would

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.199
be devastating for Luffy and the crew.

00:05:58.199 --> 00:06:02.919
They might not be able to escape or at least
if Luffy is taken out then Kizaru might go

00:06:02.919 --> 00:06:04.880
crazy attacking the rest of the crew.

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.270
And oh my god, that could lead to a seriously
bad situation for the group.

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:18.721
I could even see someone dying in this scenario,
possibly a Vegapunk or even one of the straw

00:06:18.721 --> 00:06:19.721
hats.

00:06:19.721 --> 00:06:24.100
And if this were to happen it would definitely
mean Luffy needs more power ups in the future,

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:29.100
since he will eventually have to fight to
take down the World Government.

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:34.720
And you might be thinking those are all the
options but there is actually one more possibility

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:37.250
for this fight that we haven’t discussed.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:43.699
Which is that with all of the crazy technology
here on Egghead Island someone besides Luffy

00:06:43.699 --> 00:06:46.910
may end up fighting against Kizaru.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:54.771
And in case you forgot we were actually shown
THE PERFECT WEAPONS to fight against the light

00:06:54.771 --> 00:07:00.090
fruit user at the start of the arc, when this
version of Vegapunk showed off these awesome

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:04.310
gloves that let anyone physically attack light
by punching a hologram.

00:07:04.310 --> 00:07:08.560
I mean what better way for someone without
haki to fight against the Light devil fruit

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:09.560
user?

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:16.770
And that's not all because Bonney also found
this ridiculous lightsaber that I would LOVE

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:19.280
to see actually used in a fight.

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:25.960
So could we see some of the other straw hats
fight Kizaru?

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:31.560
Or maybe even the different versions of Vegapunk
sacrificing themselves to let the straw hats

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:32.560
escape?

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.590
It is certainly possible, but if this is the
case then what other incredible event could

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.229
shock the entire world?

00:07:39.229 --> 00:07:43.680
Well, there are a few options because we have
to remember the World Government’s goal

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.630
here in the first place.

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:50.810
They came here to kill Vegapunk, but we also
recently learned that they are after the Mother

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:55.530
Flame technology, which is something that
helps them fuel the super weapon that destroyed

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.400
this entire island.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:05.490
But that doesn’t seem like world-shattering
news on its own because if Vegapunk was killed

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:11.870
the government would probably cover it up,
and the world doesn’t even know about the

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.360
Mother Flame in the first place.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.790
So if it’s not either of those, then I really
only see two other options.

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:23.639
And wow, these would both seriously shake
up the world.

00:08:23.639 --> 00:08:29.180
First, can you imagine the reaction if the
Gorosei member sent to Egghead, Saint Saturn,

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:32.370
was actually killed during this battle?

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:38.010
It would be unimaginable and likely cause
chaos in the entire world government.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:43.349
I mean we know that he has some sort of powers
from the flashback chapters at the reverie,

00:08:43.349 --> 00:08:46.870
but we don’t really know how strong he is.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:50.700
So if he gets into a fight, things could go
very bad.

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:55.270
Or the other option involves another group
of pirates who have been mysteriously missing

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.459
from these last few chapters.

00:08:57.459 --> 00:09:04.000
That’s because we saw just a glimpse of
a Blackbeard ship coming to Egghead, but assassinating

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:11.410
a member of the Gorosei is exactly the kind
of thing that they would do to cause chaos

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.410
in the world.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:16.220
And I could definitely see this happening
whether Blackbeard himself is here or if it

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:19.510
is just two of the sneakiest members of his
crew.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:25.089
Speaking of his crew, there is also the possibility
that Caterina Devon, who uses the shape-shifting

00:09:25.089 --> 00:09:31.250
Nine-Tailed fox devil fruit, could currently
be posing as an imposter on the island.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:37.140
But whether their goal is to kill the Gorosei,
steal Luffy’s poneglyph copies, or something

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:41.500
else, we will have to wait and find out.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:46.550
But the other world-shaking event that could
happen is that all of the super secret historical

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:50.580
research that Vegapunk has collected could
be shared with the world.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:56.279
I mean we know that Punk Records is basically
like the internet, so what if something happened

00:09:56.279 --> 00:10:02.150
and Vegapunk pushed a magical red button that
subscribed him to this channel for more one

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.150
Piece content…

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:08.330
Oh and it also sends all of that super secret
data to the entire world?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:13.810
This would LITERALLY be the World Government’s
worst nightmare because Vegapunk has information

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:19.459
about the Void Century and the Ancient Kingdom.

00:10:19.459 --> 00:10:25.320
And if that’s not enough to shake the world,
then I don’t know what is.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:31.380
However, while all of that is speculation
we do know that Lucci is now trying to kill

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:35.310
Vegapunk again, and Zoro has stepped up to
stop him.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:39.600
Which honestly is kinda disappointing for
both characters.

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:44.529
I mean, Lucci got washed by Luffy so now he
has to fight the second in command, and I

00:10:44.529 --> 00:10:49.850
personally feel like Zoro should handle Lucci
no problem since he has unlocked his advanced

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:51.140
conqueror’s haki.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:55.870
On the other hand, Lucci is an awakened Zoan
user now, so we’ll have to see how much

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.490
of an actual fight Oda decides to make it.

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:07.279
But really the fight I would have LOVED TO
SEE would have been Zoro against Kizaru.

00:11:07.279 --> 00:11:12.589
It surely would have been more of a challenge
than Lucci and would have pushed Zoro to his

00:11:12.589 --> 00:11:13.589
ultimate limits.

00:11:13.589 --> 00:11:17.990
And even though I desperately want to see
this fight, I don’t think Zoro would actually

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:19.630
win at his current level.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:23.560
Which also makes me wonder how Zoro is going
to grow stronger in the future.

00:11:23.560 --> 00:11:30.310
So maybe to help him fight the top tiers in
the story he might need a COMPLETELY DIFFERENT

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:33.660
powerup such as an ultra powerful devil fruit.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.980
So if you want to see just how INSANE the
story would get if Zoro ate a devil fruit,

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.760
you can watch this video right here.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:44.139
Shanks for watching and I’ll see you in
the next one.

